  "Question": "In parallelogram \\(ABCD\\), \\(\\angle A=70^\\circ\\). Find \\(\\angle B\\). Also, \\(AB=3\\). Find \\(CD\\). (Answer in order, separated by a comma, without units.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "110，3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Adjacent angles of a parallelogram are supplementary, so \\(\\angle B=180^\\circ-70^\\circ=110^\\circ\\). Opposite sides are equal, so \\(CD=AB=3\\).",
